# 29. Deployment and Runtime Provenance

Implementation is not complete after code changes.

Required where applicable:

- Production-style build
- Dist verification
- Deployment
- PM2 reload/restart only where required
- Backend port verification
- Health endpoint
- Readiness endpoint
- Worker verification
- Worker acknowledgement
- Nginx verification
- WebSocket routing
- Served bundle verification
- Runtime safety
- Log inspection

PM2 `online` alone is not proof of health.

Always distinguish Development, Staging and Production.

Do not call Staging Production.

Every closeout report must state:

- Environment
- Domain
- Source path
- Dist path
- Runtime path
- PM2 process
- Nginx target
- Runtime implementation commit
- Documentation HEAD
- Served bundle

Runtime provenance must be truthful.

A stale or misleading commit marker must be repaired or clearly explained
before claiming verified runtime.

Runtime and Git provenance must distinguish:

- Base SHA
- Feature or PR Head
- Runtime implementation commit
- Documentation Head
- Deployed backend marker
- Served frontend bundle
- Main merge commit

These values may legitimately differ.

Do not rewrite or redeploy unchanged runtime merely to make all values equal.

After a Squash Merge, the main merge commit becomes the canonical Git product
baseline, while the deployed artifact must either be rebuilt from exact main
or explicitly mapped and proven tree-equivalent during post-merge closeout.

